    '26#_': `There in Gemara and in Bava Batra Rava derives from verse.`,
    '29#_': `Chapter 1 Laws of Vows and Rabbi Natan per Beit Hillel page 71 side 1.`,
    '40#_': `There in name of Rambam chapter 1 from what we learn there taught per Shmuel, etc. page 71 side 1; holds first section is it; Ran in name of some Rishonim; and Maharshal teaches betrothed same day — if betrothed next day since did not annul day authority emptied to him — keeps her vows.`,
    '41#_': `Tur and Ran in name of Tosafot — these are Beit Shammai's words both refer; Rosh explained.`,
    '43#_': `Rambam's language chapter 1 Laws of Vows law 11 — teaches and did not hear because needs acquisition and she divorced — for reason written above seif.`,
    '47#_': `Mishnah Nedarim page 15 side 2 as Rosh, Rabbi Chananel and Rif text — halachah not as these tannaim who hold from time to time; likewise Rambam chapter 13 Laws of Vows.`,
    '48#_': `Gemara conclusion there pages 78-79 — silent intending to confirm immediately cannot annul further; see seif 71.`,
    '51#_': `Rashba in responsa and concluded there — since sage uproots vow from root — confirmation uprooted from root — annulment stands in place.`,
    '56#_': `Tur in name of Rambam chapter 2 Laws of Vows and Semag; likewise Ran in name of Ramban from question of Rami bar Chama, etc. — if you say husband annuls without hearing there page 73 side 1, etc.; holds since says if you say and cites Rabbi Zeira — appears we hold thus.`,
    '61#_': `Tur in name of Rambam there chapter 2 from question there Gemara page 73 side 1; Ravina's resolution from sotah drink, etc.; holds rabbinically plain they do not mean that specifically.`,
